If I go to the up stair (which I have to do by walking, with him
bugging me after each and every step, and frequently standing in my
way -- because it's a non-teleport level, and typically so are the
ones above and below), he either beats me there and escapes to the
level above or, if I happen to get there first, he escapes to the
level below instead.

The only way I've ever manged to kill him is to lure him to a level
that allows teleport, so I can consistently beat him to the stairs.
This can take several tries, because whether he'll escape up or down
isn't always something you can control.  Typically I have to take him
_past_ another named demon's adjascent-level non-teleport lair,
sometimes two of them, in order to get him to a normal Gehennom maze
level.

Orcus does more or less the same thing, but he's a little slower and
therefore a little easier to kill.  Also, Orcus feels more like a
challenge than a waste of time, because he's less ridiculously
ineffectual, mostly on account of being able to summon things that can
actually hurt you (potentially).

The only way Asmodeus can actually hurt you, as near as I can tell, is
by bugging you so frequently it prevents you from doing other things
that you might need to do occasionally (e.g., eating), which is just
lame.  I feel like the game would be better without him.


